{
  "name": "Splunk Security Alert Enrichment, Deduplication & Smart Notifications",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Splunk Security Alert Enrichment, Deduplication & Smart Notifications\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives Splunk alerts via webhook, then normalizes and validates each payload.\n2. Fingerprints alerts and looks up recent incidents to detect duplicates within a time window.\n3. Branches on public IPv4s to enrich with AbuseIPDB or bypass enrichment when not applicable.\n4. Calculates a risk score, stores enriched or suppressed incidents, and routes notifications by severity (email/Telegram).\n5. Generates and emails a daily 24-hour security digest from stored incidents.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure the Webhook URL in Splunk to point to the \"When Splunk Alert Received\" node’s endpoint.\n- - [ ] Set up Data Table resources/collections for incidents and suppressed incidents referenced by dataTable nodes.\n- - [ ] Add the AbuseIPDB API key to HTTP Request headers (e.g., Key: X-Api-Key) in \"Get AbuseIPDB IP Reputation\".\n- - [ ] Provide SMTP/email credentials for all Email nodes and set sender/recipients.\n- - [ ] Configure Telegram Bot API credentials and target chat/channel for the Telegram node.\n- - [ ] Define the deduplication window and fingerprint fields in the relevant Code nodes (environment variables or node params).\n- - [ ] Review and set severity thresholds used by \"Calculate Incident Risk Score\" and branching If nodes.\n- - [ ] Adjust the schedule in \"Every Day at 6 PM\" to your preferred time zone and delivery time.\n- - [ ] Use the \"Manual Setup Trigger\" once to initialize or create the incident table schema if required by your Data Table implementation.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Tune risk scoring weights and severity thresholds in the scoring code.\n- Modify fingerprint composition to better reflect your environment and alert types.\n- Customize email/Telegram templates and recipients per severity.\n- Extend enrichment to additional threat intel sources alongside AbuseIPDB.\n- Change the daily digest timeframe or include per-source sections.",
        "height": 1136,
        "width": 480
      },
